{
  "info": {
    "name": "MarketHub API",
    "description": "Multi-vendor marketplace API: auth, RBAC, vendor applications, categories, vendor product management, the public marketplace catalog, cart, checkout, orders, payments, vendor commissions/earnings, and admin payment/order management.\n\nSet `baseUrl` to your local (http://localhost:5000/api) or live backend URL. Login/register requests auto-save their token to the matching collection variable (token, adminToken, vendorToken) via a test script, so most other requests just reference {{token}} etc. directly.\n\nFor the Cart -> Checkout -> Orders flow: log in as the customer (`token`), add a couple of products from *different* vendors to the cart (so you get a real multi-vendor order), then checkout. For Vendor - Orders, log in as one of those products' vendors (`vendorToken`) -- you'll only ever see the order items that belong to that vendor, never the other vendor's lines from the same order.\n\nFor the payment flow: after Checkout, run Payments (Customer) -> Create payment, then either \"Mock: customer pays - success (webhook delivered)\" or the no-webhook variant followed by \"Verify payment\". Paying an order is what moves it from PENDING to CONFIRMED and creates the vendors' commissions; vendors cannot advance an unpaid order. To use the Webhook requests, set the `webhookSecret` collection variable to PAYMENT_WEBHOOK_SECRET from backend/.env (it is left empty on purpose). The Admin folders need `adminToken` (Auth -> Login as Admin).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:5000/api" },
    { "key": "token", "value": "" },
    { "key": "adminToken", "value": "" },
    { "key": "vendorToken", "value": "" },
    { "key": "categoryId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "vendorApplicationId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "productId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "cartItemId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "orderId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "paymentId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "transactionId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "paymentAmount", "value": "" },
    { "key": "webhookSecret", "value": "" },
    { "key": "webhookEventId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "webhookBody", "value": "" },
    { "key": "webhookSignature", "value": "" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register (customer)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/register",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Test Customer\",\n  \"email\": \"customer@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"pass1234\"\n}"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Login (saves token)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "  const data = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('token', data.token);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"customer@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"pass1234\"\n}"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Login as Admin (saves adminToken)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "  const data = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('adminToken', data.token);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"admin@test.com\",\n  \"password\": \"<SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD from backend/.env>\"\n}"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Login as Vendor (saves vendorToken)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "  const data = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('vendorToken', data.token);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"vendor@test.com\",\n  \"password\": \"<SEED_VENDOR_PASSWORD from backend/.env>\"\n}"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Current user (/me)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{token}}" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/me"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Logout",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{token}}" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/logout"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Role Dashboards (Day 1 demo routes)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Customer dashboard",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{token}}" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/customer/dashboard"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Vendor dashboard",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{vendorToken}}" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/vendor/dashboard"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Admin dashboard",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{adminToken}}" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/admin/dashboard"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Vendor Applications",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Apply as vendor (customer only)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{token}}" }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/vendors",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"storeName\": \"My Store\",\n  \"storeDescription\": \"What this store sells\",\n  \"logo\": \"https://example.com/logo.png\"\n}"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "My application status",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{token}}" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/vendors/me"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "List approved stores (public)",
          "request": { "method": "GET", "url": "{{baseUrl}}/vendors" }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get store by id (public)",
          "request": { "method": "GET", "url": "{{baseUrl}}/vendors/:id" }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Admin - Vendor Management",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List vendor applications",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{adminToken}}" }],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/admin/vendors?status=PENDING",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["admin", "vendors"],
              "query": [{ "key": "status", "value": "PENDING", "description": "PENDING | APPROVED | SUSPENDED | REJECTED (optional)" }]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get vendor application by id",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{adminToken}}" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/admin/vendors/{{vendorApplicationId}}"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Approve vendor",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{adminToken}}" }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/admin/vendors/{{vendorApplicationId}}/status",
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"status\": \"APPROVED\"\n}" }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Reject vendor",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{adminToken}}" }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/admin/vendors/{{vendorApplicationId}}/status",
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"status\": \"REJECTED\"\n}" }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Suspend vendor",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{adminToken}}" }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/admin/vendors/{{vendorApplicationId}}/status",
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"status\": \"SUSPENDED\"\n}" }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Categories",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List categories (public)",
          "request": { "method": "GET", "url": "{{baseUrl}}/categories" }
        },
        {
          "name": "Create category (admin)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('categoryId', pm.response.json().category._id);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{adminToken}}" }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/categories",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Electronics\",\n  \"description\": \"Phones, laptops and gadgets\"\n}"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Update category (admin)",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{adminToken}}" }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/categories/{{categoryId}}",
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"description\": \"Updated description\"\n}" }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Delete category (admin)",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{adminToken}}" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/categories/{{categoryId}}"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Vendor - My Products",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create product",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('productId', pm.response.json().product._id);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{vendorToken}}" }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/vendor/products",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Wireless Mouse\",\n  \"description\": \"Ergonomic wireless mouse\",\n  \"price\": 19.99,\n  \"stock\": 50,\n  \"category\": \"{{categoryId}}\",\n  \"images\": [\"https://example.com/mouse.png\"],\n  \"status\": \"DRAFT\"\n}"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "List my products",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{vendorToken}}" }],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/vendor/products?status=ACTIVE",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["vendor", "products"],
              "query": [{ "key": "status", "value": "ACTIVE", "description": "DRAFT | ACTIVE | OUT_OF_STOCK | ARCHIVED (optional)" }]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get my product by id",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{vendorToken}}" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/vendor/products/{{productId}}"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Update my product / publish",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{vendorToken}}" }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/vendor/products/{{productId}}",
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"status\": \"ACTIVE\"\n}" }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Update stock",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{vendorToken}}" }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/vendor/products/{{productId}}",
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"stock\": 0\n}" }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Archive product (soft delete)",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{vendorToken}}" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/vendor/products/{{productId}}"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Public Marketplace",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Browse products (search, filter, sort, paginate)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/products?search=mouse&category=electronics&minPrice=5&maxPrice=50&sort=price_asc&page=1&limit=12",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["products"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "search", "value": "mouse" },
                { "key": "category", "value": "electronics", "description": "category slug or id" },
                { "key": "vendor", "value": "", "description": "vendor id", "disabled": true },
                { "key": "minPrice", "value": "5" },
                { "key": "maxPrice", "value": "50" },
                { "key": "sort", "value": "price_asc", "description": "newest | price_asc | price_desc" },
                { "key": "page", "value": "1" },
                { "key": "limit", "value": "12", "description": "max 50" }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get product by id",
          "request": { "method": "GET", "url": "{{baseUrl}}/products/{{productId}}" }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Cart",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Add item to cart",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
                  "  const item = pm.response.json().cart.items.find((i) => i.product.id === pm.collectionVariables.get('productId'));",
                  "  if (item) pm.collectionVariables.set('cartItemId', item.id);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{token}}" }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/cart/items",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"productId\": \"{{productId}}\",\n  \"quantity\": 2\n}"
            },
            "description": "Adding a product already in the cart increases its quantity instead of creating a duplicate row. Add products from two different vendors (different productId values) to build a multi-vendor cart."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "View cart",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{token}}" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/cart",
            "description": "Items are grouped by vendor. Each item may carry an `issue` (e.g. out of stock, vendor no longer approved) -- prices always come from the current product record, never from anything the client sent."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Update cart item quantity",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{token}}" }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/cart/items/{{cartItemId}}",
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"quantity\": 3\n}" }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Remove cart item",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{token}}" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/cart/items/{{cartItemId}}"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Checkout",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Checkout (create order from cart)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('orderId', pm.response.json().order.id);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{token}}" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/checkout",
            "description": "Re-validates every cart item inside a database transaction (still exists, ACTIVE, vendor APPROVED, enough stock), using DB prices only. On success: creates the order and its items, decrements stock, and clears the cart, all atomically. On failure: a 400 with an `errors` array naming which items are the problem -- nothing is created or changed."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Orders (Customer)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List my orders",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{token}}" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/orders"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get my order by id",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{token}}" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}",
            "description": "Returns 404 (not 403) for an order that exists but belongs to someone else -- existence isn't leaked."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Vendor - Orders",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List orders containing my products",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{vendorToken}}" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/vendor/orders",
            "description": "Each entry is grouped by order, but `items` and `vendorSubtotal` only ever include this vendor's own lines -- another vendor's products in the same order are never visible here."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get one order (my items only)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{vendorToken}}" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/vendor/orders/{{orderId}}",
            "description": "404 if this order has none of your products, even if the order itself exists for another vendor."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Update fulfillment status",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{vendorToken}}" }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/vendor/orders/{{orderId}}/status",
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"status\": \"PROCESSING\"\n}" },
            "description": "Only moves your own items, and only once the order is PAID (400 \"not been paid yet\" otherwise; payment already moves a paid order's items to CONFIRMED). Cancelling returns the stock and voids the commission. Allowed values: CONFIRMED, PROCESSING, SHIPPED, DELIVERED, CANCELLED. Must move forward one step at a time (PENDING -> CONFIRMED -> PROCESSING -> SHIPPED -> DELIVERED); CANCELLED is allowed from any non-terminal state. The order's overall status (visible to the customer) always reflects whichever vendor segment is the least far along."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Payments (Customer)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create payment for my order (saves paymentId, transactionId)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
                  "  const { payment } = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('paymentId', payment.id);",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('transactionId', payment.transactionId);",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('paymentAmount', payment.amount);",
                  "}",
                  "pm.test(\"Status is 201\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/payments/create",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"orderId\": \"{{orderId}}\"\n}"
            },
            "description": "Only the order id is sent -- the amount is always read from the order in the database. 404 for an order that isn't yours, 409 if it is already paid, 400 if it is cancelled. Calling it again for the same order returns the same open payment (no duplicates). A FAILED or expired payment lets you create a fresh one."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get latest payment for my order",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "  const { payment } = pm.response.json();",
                  "  if (payment) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('paymentId', payment.id);",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('transactionId', payment.transactionId);",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('paymentAmount', payment.amount);",
                  "  }",
                  "}",
                  "pm.test(\"Status is 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/payments/order/{{orderId}}",
            "description": "The newest payment attempt for one of your orders (what the payment page uses after a refresh), or `{ \"payment\": null }` if none has been started -- also what you get for someone else's order, so existence isn't leaked."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Verify payment (provider is asked, not the browser)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status is 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/payments/verify",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"transactionId\": \"{{transactionId}}\"\n}"
            },
            "description": "The server asks the payment provider for the real status and checks the amount and order match. PAID -> order becomes CONFIRMED. Safe to call repeatedly (already-settled payments just return their state). Before the customer has paid it stays PENDING."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Mock: customer pays - success (webhook delivered)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status is 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/payments/mock/pay",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"transactionId\": \"{{transactionId}}\",\n  \"outcome\": \"success\"\n}"
            },
            "description": "Development only (PAYMENT_PROVIDER=mock; 404 otherwise). Stands in for the customer paying on the provider's page. The provider then sends a signed webhook, so the payment is PAID straight away."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Mock: customer pays - success, webhook NOT delivered",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status is 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/payments/mock/pay",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"transactionId\": \"{{transactionId}}\",\n  \"outcome\": \"success\",\n  \"deliverWebhook\": false\n}"
            },
            "description": "Same as above but our server is NOT told. The payment stays PENDING until you call \"Verify payment\", which asks the provider and settles it (what happens when a webhook is late or lost)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Mock: customer pays - failure",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status is 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/payments/mock/pay",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"transactionId\": \"{{transactionId}}\",\n  \"outcome\": \"failure\"\n}"
            },
            "description": "Payment becomes FAILED and the order stays PENDING (not confirmed). Create a new payment for the same order to retry."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Webhook - signed success event (provider -> server)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const secret = pm.collectionVariables.get('webhookSecret');",
                  "if (!secret) throw new Error('Set the webhookSecret collection variable to PAYMENT_WEBHOOK_SECRET from backend/.env');",
                  "const eventId = 'evt_' + Date.now();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('webhookEventId', eventId);",
                  "const body = JSON.stringify({",
                  "  id: eventId,",
                  "  type: 'payment.succeeded',",
                  "  data: {",
                  "    transactionId: pm.collectionVariables.get('transactionId'),",
                  "    orderId: pm.collectionVariables.get('orderId'),",
                  "    amount: Number(pm.collectionVariables.get('paymentAmount')),",
                  "    currency: 'USD',",
                  "  },",
                  "});",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('webhookBody', body);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('webhookSignature', CryptoJS.HmacSHA256(body, secret).toString());"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status is 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test(\"received\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().received).to.eql(true));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "x-payment-signature",
                "value": "{{webhookSignature}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/payments/webhook",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{{webhookBody}}"
            },
            "description": "Called by the provider, not by a user -- no Authorization header. The pre-request script builds the event and signs it (HMAC-SHA256) with the `webhookSecret` collection variable: paste PAYMENT_WEBHOOK_SECRET from backend/.env there. Needs `transactionId`, `orderId` and `paymentAmount` from \"Create payment\". This only simulates the provider's call: the mock provider itself is not told the customer paid, so a payment settled this way can't be refunded later. To try the refund, pay with a \"Mock: customer pays - success\" request instead."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Webhook - replay the same event (no effect)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const secret = pm.collectionVariables.get('webhookSecret');",
                  "if (!secret) throw new Error('Set the webhookSecret collection variable to PAYMENT_WEBHOOK_SECRET from backend/.env');",
                  "const eventId = pm.collectionVariables.get('webhookEventId');",
                  "if (!eventId) throw new Error('Run \"Webhook - signed success event\" first so there is an event to replay');",
                  "const body = JSON.stringify({",
                  "  id: eventId,",
                  "  type: 'payment.succeeded',",
                  "  data: {",
                  "    transactionId: pm.collectionVariables.get('transactionId'),",
                  "    orderId: pm.collectionVariables.get('orderId'),",
                  "    amount: Number(pm.collectionVariables.get('paymentAmount')),",
                  "    currency: 'USD',",
                  "  },",
                  "});",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('webhookBody', body);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('webhookSignature', CryptoJS.HmacSHA256(body, secret).toString());"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status is 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "x-payment-signature",
                "value": "{{webhookSignature}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/payments/webhook",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{{webhookBody}}"
            },
            "description": "Re-sends the exact event from the previous request. Still 200 (so the provider stops retrying) but nothing changes: paidAt stays the same and the event is processed only once."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Webhook - invalid signature (expect 400)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const secret = pm.collectionVariables.get('webhookSecret');",
                  "if (!secret) throw new Error('Set the webhookSecret collection variable to PAYMENT_WEBHOOK_SECRET from backend/.env');",
                  "const eventId = 'evt_' + Date.now();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('webhookEventId', eventId);",
                  "const body = JSON.stringify({",
                  "  id: eventId,",
                  "  type: 'payment.succeeded',",
                  "  data: {",
                  "    transactionId: pm.collectionVariables.get('transactionId'),",
                  "    orderId: pm.collectionVariables.get('orderId'),",
                  "    amount: Number(pm.collectionVariables.get('paymentAmount')),",
                  "    currency: 'USD',",
                  "  },",
                  "});",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('webhookBody', body);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('webhookSignature', CryptoJS.HmacSHA256(body, secret).toString());"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status is 400\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "x-payment-signature",
                "value": "deadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeef"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/payments/webhook",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{{webhookBody}}"
            },
            "description": "A request that is not signed with the shared secret is rejected, so nobody can fake a \"payment done\" event."
          }
        }
      ]
